/-!
# The cusp-condition codimension is at most the cusp double-coset count

Theorem statement: `MTT.Cohomology.finrank_modularForm_le_cuspForm_add_doubleCosets`
(`9f6c61f4-df4d-4542-88d1-63a18b965ed7`), by cbirkbeck, 2026-09-07.

Proof: submission `ea21976d-818a-4d31-ad2f-32109d027672`, by cbirkbeck, 2026-09-07 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

Let $H$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ and let $k\in\mathbb Z$. Let $T$ be
the translation matrix and put $P_\infty=\langle T,-I\rangle$. Then

$$\dim_{\mathbb C} M_k(H)\le\dim_{\mathbb C} S_k(H)+\#(H\backslash\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb
Z)/P_\infty).$$

This elementary codimension bound converts a modular-form dimension lower bound into a cusp-form
lower bound. It is used in the higher-weight Gamma1 dimension branch of the MTT mission. No equality
or cohomology comparison is asserted.

## Explanation of the source proof

For a finite-index subgroup H of SL₂(ℤ), choose one representative of every H-orbit of rational
cusps and a matrix carrying infinity to that representative. Take the constant term of the
corresponding slash translate. These are complex-linear functionals: the q-expansion at every
arithmetic cusp converges to a limit, and limits commute with addition and scalar multiplication.
Their joint kernel is precisely the cusp-form subspace, since vanishing is independent of the
representative within an H-orbit. Rank-nullity therefore bounds dim M_k(H) by dim S_k(H) plus the
number of cusp orbits.

The double-coset space H\SL₂(ℤ)/⟨T,-I⟩ surjects onto those cusp orbits, because T and -I fix
infinity. It is finite, as a quotient of the finite coset space H\SL₂(ℤ). This gives the exact
double-coset-count form of the bound.

Source: Marc Masdeu, Modular Forms, Chapter 5, §5.1, the cusp-evaluation discussion preceding Lemma
5.2 and the codimension formulas in Theorem 5.1,
https://mmasdeu.github.io/modularforms/5_eisenstein.html. The submitted statement proves only the
elementary upper bound on codimension, not the stronger Eisenstein dimension equalities. The
argument generalizes this bound from congruence subgroups to all finite-index subgroups and
arbitrary integral weights.

The proof uses mathlib's actual modular forms, cusp forms, cusp orbits and slash actions. The only
imported platform theorem is the already-PROVED ModularForm.finiteDimensional_of_isArithmetic
(fec292ab-0757-5b48-a9bc-a13e34bc1b49). The new kernel and cusp-count comparison lemmas have
standard axiom closures. No sorry, custom axiom, native_decide, or resource-limit override appears
in this submission.

MTT role: combines the existing higher-weight Gamma1 modular-form dimension lower bound with the
cusp-condition codimension bound, giving the independent cusp-form lower bound needed by the
higher-level parabolic-cohomology comparison. It does not assert the still-open cohomological upper
bound.

